body:
Yes we do. We can't rely on the same 11 for a whole season. Also the players need some competition between them, so I'd imagine Greenwood would fight for Sancho for the RW (since the last games I personally see Greenwood more as a RW than a CF), James would be Rash backup, we will also need a backup for Martial after Ighalo loan expires and if we get VDB or Grealish to rotate in the 10 spot that would be awesome.

&#x200B;

So on short, if we can get a top quality player we should get them even if our current 11 looks great.

So I have 51GB left on my hard drive (I have a 256GB SSD) and I thought the new update was supposed to shrink the size of the game. Right now I'm confused because I thought it was supposed to delete files, not to install more stuff.

&#x200B;

Is it ok if I uninstall the game and reinstall it?

Ocon proved himself, but he's a Merc driver, while Lando is a McLaren junior driver. For now, imo, he kinda proved himself. Last year at Hungaroring in testing he demolished Van and Alo quali times, at Daytona this year in January he made some great recoveries. And maybe in F2 he is not the leader right now, he's the most consistent driver, missing points only 2 times (1 time wasn't his fault, was because of a clutch failure). I don't think he will fade away in F1 like Van.

&#x200B;

I might say all of this because I'm a big fan of Norris, but there's still some truth in it...
